# Additional interpolation values for the THREE-file local stack. Start with
# self-hosted.env.example, including its operations values; do not load into API.
# Supply private files outside the checkout. Never publish compose config output.
ODDPATH_WEB_IMAGE=oddpath-web:reviewed
ODDPATH_NGINX_IMAGE=nginx@sha256:<reviewed-multiarch-digest>
ODDPATH_HTTPS_PORT=8443
ODDPATH_APP_HOST=app.oddpath.test
ODDPATH_API_HOST=api.oddpath.test
ODDPATH_VIEWER_HOST=browser.oddpath.test
ODDPATH_API_ORIGIN=https://api.oddpath.test:8443
ODDPATH_VIEWER_ORIGIN=https://browser.oddpath.test:8443
ODDPATH_R2_ORIGIN=
ODDPATH_TLS_CHAIN_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/tls-chain.pem
ODDPATH_TLS_KEY_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/tls-key.pem
ODDPATH_CONTROL_CA_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/control-ca.pem
ODDPATH_SUPERVISOR_IMAGE=oddpath-browser-supervisor:reviewed
ODDPATH_SUPERVISOR_CONTAINER=oddpath-rehearsal-supervisor
ODDPATH_SUPERVISOR_CONFIG_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/supervisor.json
ODDPATH_VIEWER_KEY_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/viewer-key
ODDPATH_ROUTING_KEY_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/routing-key
ODDPATH_TRANSFER_KEYRING_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/transfer-keyring.json
ODDPATH_VAULT_KEYRING_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/vault-keyring.json
ODDPATH_VAULT_VOLUME=oddpath-rehearsal-vault
ODDPATH_BROWSER_JOURNAL_VOLUME=oddpath-rehearsal-browser-journal

# Provision BOTH new volumes explicitly; never use an existing user-data volume.
# vault volume: private0700 owned by API image node UID1000; shared ONLY by API
# and API reaper. Storage ciphertext remains in PostgreSQL; this volume contains
# the independently current MAC-protected revocation journal, including SQLite
# WAL/SHM files. It is not a second copy of PostgreSQL.
# browser journal: private0700 owned by the trusted supervisor UID (currently0),
# shared only by supervisor/runtime reaper. Never mount it into tenant Chrome.
# TLS private key must be0600 owned/readable by ingress UID101 on Linux. Keyrings
# must be private/readable by their exact container UID; Compose mode fields
# do not fix host bind permissions. API alone gets storage/revocation keys;
# supervisor gets transfer keys only. Never mount full keyrings into Chrome.
# API env needs the separate viewer/routing/project keys if subsequently enabled;
# supervisor config and API values must agree. Do not put keys in this template.
# Distinct app/API/viewer hostnames are mandatory. API/viewer hostname changes
# require rebuilding web, because its API URL and CSP are immutable build inputs.
# Internal discovery should use https://<API_HOST>:8443 (the gateway control
# network alias). Its CA chain is validated through NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS.
# supervisorContainer must exactly match ODDPATH_SUPERVISOR_CONTAINER; chromeImage
# and egressImage must be sha256 image IDs, per the existing runtime config schema.
# publicOrigin is the exact viewer origin; viewerFrameOrigin is the app origin.
# Use discovery {serverUrl,keyFile:'/run/secrets/managed_routing_key'}, allowManualLogin
# and allowSavedLogin only with separately reviewed API activation. The current
# production guard still rejects v2; --profile browser is not an override.
#
# Build/boot (explicit private --env-file, three -f files, unique -p project):
# docker compose --env-file <private.env> -p <rehearsal> \
#   -f deploy/self-hosted.compose.yml -f deploy/self-hosted.operations.compose.yml \
#   -f deploy/self-hosted.stack.compose.yml config --quiet
# Bootstrap PostgreSQL roles, run migrate once, recheck grants, then start api
# and gateway. Select --profile maintenance / --profile backup only after their
# own volume/credential bootstrap. The browser profile remains activation-gated.
# The only published port is loopback HTTPS; API, PostgreSQL, CDP and VNC have no
# host bindings. This is no external deployment, DNS change or certificate issue.
#
# Closed DB-only backups KEEP refusing runtime/vault/object data. A complete
# encrypted multi-component backup/restore, independent revocation/deletion/
# accounting continuity, off-host copy and alert delivery remain open gates.
# Never remove that refusal, restore SQLite journals from an old DB snapshot,
# reset a journal/fence, or release reservations to make rehearsal health pass.
# The existing restore CLI writes restore-status.json beside the supplied archive;
# use a private writable recovery directory, keeping the independent off-host copy
# intact. A lost final acknowledgement requires target inspection, not overwriting
# or blindly retrying restoration against a populated target.

# OPTIONAL account-limited production rehearsal, pending independent acceptance.
# Add -f deploy/self-hosted.closed-browser.compose.yml after the stack overlay.
# ODDPATH_CLOSED_REHEARSAL_OWNER_IDS=synthetic-owner-id
# This is an exact 1–20-account list, not emails/wildcards; no accounts are created.
# Select --profile browser only after image/key/volume/role prerequisites.
# API and api-reaper share the mode/list; NODE_ENV stays production.
# Base defaults, public registration, paid AI, saved state and private assets stay
# gated. See apps/browser-runtime/README.md Closed production rehearsal.
